So `ZonedDateTime.parse(isoString, ISO_FORMAT)` handles both cases: input with offset "+0000" → ZonedDateTime with that offset; input without offset → systemDefault zone. That matches SimpleDateFormat behavior most closely (SimpleDateFormat without offset would use default tz for fields... well, it defaults missing fields; offset missing → uses default tz).

But ZonedDateTime.parse requires all fields of the pattern (date, time, fraction). SimpleDateFormat lenient mode allowed missing stuff, but that's edge behavior not worth preserving.

